  "response": "**VERDICT: REVISE**\n\n**Overall Assessment**: The carousel implements basic interactive controls with native `<button>` elements, which is a strong foundation. However, it fails to communicate dynamic state changes to assistive technology, lacks region context, and omits standard keyboard navigation patterns required by the WAI-ARIA APG Slideshow pattern. Screen reader users will not know when slides change or which indicator is active, and keyboard users are restricted to tab-only navigation without arrow key support.\n\n**Pre-commitment Predictions**: \nBefore reading the code, I predicted: (1) missing `aria-live` region for dynamic slide updates, (2) missing `role=\"region\"`/label on the carousel container, (3) missing `aria-current` on active indicators, (4) lack of arrow key keyboard navigation, and (5) dynamic `alt` text without programmatic announcement. All predictions materialized during review.\n\n**Critical Findings** (blocks access):\n1. **Missing `aria-live` region for dynamic slide changes**\n   - Evidence: `BuggyCarousel.jsx:28` (`<img src={images[currentIndex]} alt={`Carousel image ${currentIndex + 1}`} />`)\n   - User group impacted: Screen reader users\n   - WCAG/APG citation: WCAG 4.1.3 (Status Messages), WAI-ARIA APG Slideshow pattern\n   - Why this matters: Changing the `alt` attribute on an `<img>` does not trigger screen reader announcements. Users will hear nothing when the slide changes, breaking the core interaction model.\n   - Fix: Add a visually hidden live region that announces position context: `<div aria-live=\"polite\" className=\"sr-only\">Image {currentIndex + 1} of {images.length}</div>` placed inside the carousel container.\n\n2. **Missing `role=\"region\"` and accessible name on carousel container**\n   - Evidence: `BuggyCarousel.jsx:25` (`<div className=\"carousel\">`)\n   - User group impacted: Screen reader users, keyboard users\n   - WCAG/APG citation: WCAG 4.1.2 (Name, Role, Value), WAI-ARIA APG Slideshow pattern\n   - Why this matters: Without `role=\"region\"` and an `aria-label`, assistive technology treats the carousel as a generic container with no semantic context or landmark navigation support.\n   - Fix: Update to `<div className=\"carousel\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"Image carousel\">`.\n\n**Major Findings** (significantly degrades experience):\n1. **Missing `aria-current` on active indicator button**\n   - Evidence: `BuggyCarousel.jsx:35-40` (`className={idx === currentIndex ? 'active' : ''}`)\n   - User group impacted: Screen reader users, cognitive accessibility users\n   - WCAG/APG citation: WCAG 4.1.2 (Name, Role, Value), WAI-ARIA APG Slideshow pattern\n   - Why this matters: Indicators visually highlight the current slide but provide no programmatic state to assistive technology. Screen reader users cannot determine which slide is active by navigating the indicators.\n   - Fix: Add `aria-current={idx === currentIndex ? 'true' : undefined}` to each indicator `<button>`.\n\n2. **No keyboard navigation for Prev/Next controls**\n   - Evidence: `BuggyCarousel.jsx:10-17` (`onClick={goToPrevious}`, `onClick={goToNext}`)\n   - User group impacted: Keyboard-only users, motor accessibility users\n   - WCAG/APG citation: WCAG 2.1.1 (Keyboard), WAI-ARIA APG Slideshow pattern\n   - Why this matters: Standard carousel interaction expects arrow keys for navigation. Relying solely on `onClick` forces keyboard users to tab through every control and breaks expected widget conventions.\n   - Fix: Add `onKeyDown` handlers to the container or buttons: `ArrowLeft`/`ArrowRight` trigger prev/next, `Home` jumps to first slide, `End` jumps to last slide. Ensure `event.preventDefault()` is called for these keys.\n\n```\n### A11y Evidence Finding\nfinding_id: carousel-missing-live-region\nfingerprint: a7f3c9d2e1b4\nsource: BuggyCarousel.jsx:28\nwcag_or_apg: WCAG 4.1.3, WAI-ARIA APG Slideshow pattern\nsection_508_fpc_context: not in scope\nseverity: CRITICAL\nperspective_alarms: screen reader=HIGH\nevidence: DOM excerpt shows dynamic alt on img without aria-live region or focus movement\nreproduction_steps: 1. Mount component with >1 image. 2. Use screen reader to navigate to carousel. 3. Click Next button.\nexpected_behavior: Screen reader announces \"Image 2 of 5\" or equivalent position context.\nactual_behavior: No announcement; alt attribute changes silently in DOM.\ntrend: new\n```\n\n**Minor Findings** (friction but workaround exists):\n- Dynamic `alt` text (`Carousel image ${currentIndex + 1}`) is functionally redundant when paired with a proper live region. Per WCAG 1.1.1, `alt` should describe the *image content*, not its position. Consider static descriptive alt per slide or rely on the live region for positional context.\n- Indicator buttons lack visible focus indicators in CSS (not shown in snippet, but standard expectation). Ensure `:focus-visible` outlines meet WCAG 2.4.13 (3:1 contrast change, 2px perimeter).\n\n**What's Missing** (gaps, unhandled edge cases, unstated assumptions):\n- Missing pause/play control: If the carousel auto-rotates (common pattern), it requires a pause button with `aria-pressed` state and must respect `prefers-reduced-motion`.\n- Missing keyboard trap prevention for dynamic content: When slides change, focus remains on the clicked button. This is acceptable if live region handles announcements, but focus should not jump unexpectedly.\n- Missing landmark/heading context: The carousel lacks a heading or descriptive wrapper that ties it to surrounding page content.\n\n**Multi-Perspective Notes**:\n- **Screen reader user**: Hears button labels (\"Previous\", \"Next\") and indicator numbers, but receives no announcement when slides change. Cannot determine current slide via indicators due to missing `aria-current`. Region has no accessible name.\n- **Keyboard-only user**: Can tab to buttons and activate them with Enter/Space. Cannot use arrow keys for navigation (breaks APG convention). Focus stays on trigger button after click, which is acceptable but lacks keyboard discoverability.\n- **Low vision user**: Buttons are native and likely meet target size if styled properly. Needs visible focus indicators on all interactive elements. Dynamic layout shifts should be avoided or announced.\n- **Cognitive accessibility**: Visual indicator highlights current slide, but AT users lack equivalent state communication. Error states (e.g., empty `images` array) are unhandled and would render broken UI without fallback messaging.\n\n**Verdict Justification**: The component passes basic automated checks (native buttons, present alt text) but fails core assistive technology interaction requirements. The absence of an `aria-live` region and region labeling creates a complete access barrier for screen reader users regarding dynamic state changes. Missing `aria-current` and keyboard navigation degrade the experience for multiple user groups. These are not preference issues; they are structural gaps in the WAI-ARIA APG Slideshow pattern implementation. The design must be revised before shipping.\n\n**Open Questions (unscored)**:\n- Does the carousel auto-rotate? If yes, a pause/play control with `aria-pressed` is required per APG.\n- Are indicator buttons visually styled to clearly show active state for low-vision users without relying solely on color?\n- Is the `images` array guaranteed to be non-empty? Consider adding `role=\"status\"` or fallback messaging when `images.length === 0`.",
